From: Davíð Steinn Geirsson <david@dsg.is>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: set the MTU before reopening on a running change

stmmac_change_mtu() reopens a running interface with DMA buffers sized
for the new MTU, but only updates dev->mtu after __stmmac_open()
returns. The reopen reprograms the MAC through stmmac_core_init(), and
dwmac1000_core_init() derives GMAC_CONTROL_2K and GMAC_CONTROL_JE from
dev->mtu, so it sees the old value: raising the MTU of a running
interface to a jumbo size leaves jumbo frame reception disabled until
the next down/up.

Set dev->mtu before the reopen and restore it if the reopen fails.

Signed-off-by: Davíð Steinn Geirsson <david@dsg.is>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
@@ -5959,6 +5959,7 @@ static int stmmac_change_mtu(struct net_
 	struct stmmac_priv *priv = netdev_priv(dev);
 	int txfifosz = priv->plat->tx_fifo_size;
 	struct stmmac_dma_conf *dma_conf;
+	const int old_mtu = dev->mtu;
 	const int mtu = new_mtu;
 	int ret;
 
@@ -5990,8 +5991,11 @@ static int stmmac_change_mtu(struct net_
 
 		__stmmac_release(dev);
 
+		/* The core init on reopen programs the MAC from dev->mtu */
+		WRITE_ONCE(dev->mtu, mtu);
 		ret = __stmmac_open(dev, dma_conf);
 		if (ret) {
+			WRITE_ONCE(dev->mtu, old_mtu);
 			free_dma_desc_resources(priv, dma_conf);
 			kfree(dma_conf);
 			netdev_err(priv->dev, "failed reopening the interface after MTU change\n");
